Portions of the presentation semantics in the thought (reasoning) block —
collapsed-by-default streaming with a latest-line summary, auto-collapse on
stream end unless the user interacted, content scroll-follow with a bottom
lock, and a host-supplied real duration label — are derived from the
vercel/ai-elements `reasoning.tsx` component:

  Original: packages/elements/src/reasoning.tsx
  Copyright 2023 Vercel, Inc.
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
  https://github.com/vercel/ai-elements

The derived behavior was reimplemented from scratch in plain ESM with no
source copied; the original Apache-2.0 notice is retained here per the
license's redistribution terms. No "inspired by" product branding is asserted.

The execute/read/edit renderer contracts and the unified-diff line-number
parsing are adapted from the ZCode DESKTOP task conversation presentation
(also Apache-2.0 within this reference set): execute `$` prompt + bounded
command and safe-ANSI stdout/stderr/exit/cwd, read file chip, edit file chips
with +N/-N count and inline diff carrying real @@ line numbers. These were
reimplemented as pure, function-free view-model fragments; the Markdown table adaptation described below includes derived source.


The reasoning summary playback queue is adapted from
packages/ui/src/ToolCallBlocks/QueuedSummaryContent.tsx and the latest-line
selection in packages/ui/src/components/ai-elements/reasoning.tsx of ZCode,
revision 3c5b227649371507ddc4eb46ac5133afe6db1cab, under Apache-2.0.
This distribution changes the implementation to a host-independent ESM
scheduler and CSS transitions; it retains no dependency on that application.

Inline tool and reasoning icons contain Lucide SVG paths from lucide-static 0.544.0.

